      <h2 id="insights-operator-showing-data-collected-from-the-cluster_showing-data-collected-by-remote-health-monitoring" class="group scroll-mt-20">Showing data collected by the Insights Operator<a href="#insights-operator-showing-data-collected-from-the-cluster_showing-data-collected-by-remote-health-monitoring" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can review the data that is collected by the Insights Operator.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>Access to the cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Find the name of the currently running pod for the Insights Operator:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ INSIGHTS_OPERATOR_POD=$(oc get pods --namespace=openshift-insights -o custom-columns=:metadata.name --no-headers  --field-selector=status.phase=Running)"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Copy the recent data archives collected by the Insights Operator:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc cp openshift-insights/$INSIGHTS_OPERATOR_POD:/var/lib/insights-operator ./insights-data"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The recent Insights Operator archives are now available in the <code>insights-data</code> directory.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
